<h2>Motivation and Approach</h2>

<p class="lead-text">
    The ability to think like a geoscientist is increasingly important in our society. The global challenges of this century &ndash; climate change, water scarcity, stress on our food system &ndash; are almost all geologically related. Through teaching in the classroom, in the field, and by involving students in active research, I hope to educate the next generation of global citizens in our deeply interconnected Earth system.
</p>

<p class="lead-text">
    I use a quantitative, data-driven approach to teaching that gets students working with real geologic data, interacting with physical phenomena in activities and labs, and collecting and analyzing the geologic record on field trips. I hope students leave my classes with a firm understanding of how we observe our world, go about analyzing data, and make well-supported interpretations.
</p>

